  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1243 PM CDT Fri Jul 17 2026\n\nWV imagery indicates a broad upper level ridge of high pressure \nlocked in across the Western High Plains. Near the surface, a weak \nlee side trough of low pressure remains anchored in eastern Colorado.\n\nRelatively dry conditions will persist early in the period with the \nSREF indicating very little change to the aforementioned pattern \nacross the region. An extremely weak flow aloft combined with \nmarginal instability/deep layer shear will keep precip chances at \nbay for the most part through the weekend. Near seasonal temperatures\nare forecast tonight with lows in the 60s(F) to the lower 70s(F).\nA gradual warming trend is likely through the weekend as high pressure\ndominates aloft while prevailing southerlies continue to draw warmer\nair into the area, pushing H85 temperatures up around 25C in central\nKansas to near 30C in vicinity of the Colorado line Saturday. Look\nfor widespread afternoon highs in the 90s(F) with the HREF indicating\na 70-90% probability of temperatures exceeding 90F. Expect highs\npushing 100F by early next week.",
